    clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8974: Use the M/N counter for camera MCLKs
    
    The MCLK0-3 tables contain fractional rates, but their RCG descriptions
    leave mnd_width at zero. The shared RCG code consequently skips M/N
    programming and readback. For example, the 24 MHz entry with a 600 MHz
    GPLL0 parent produces 120 MHz after its divide-by-five stage instead of
    applying the additional 1/5 fraction.
    
    Declare the eight-bit M/N counters for all four MCLK RCGs. This restores
    the fractional entries shared by MSM8974 and the MSM8226 override tables
    without changing their parent maps or requested frequencies.
    
    An extracted-production ASan/UBSan host reproducer shows 22 mismatches
    among 50 table cases before the change and none afterward. All four
    per-clock omission controls reproduce the 120 MHz result. Native ARM
    and ARM64 COMPILE_TEST component validation is recorded separately; no
    new hardware acceptance is claimed by this refresh.
    
    Fixes: d8b212014e69 ("clk: qcom: Add support for MSM8974's multimedia clock controller (MMCC)")
    
    Original integration work by Timothy Schmidt credits Claude Opus 5.5
    <noreply@anthropic.com> as co-author. This current-base refresh and host
    qualification used OpenAI Codex. Human review and DCO remain pending.

